coefficients(LieElement) -- get the coefficients and monomials of a Lie element
*******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note coefficients: (Macaulay2Doc)coefficients,
  * Usage: 
        c = coefficients(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,, $x$ is of
        type $L$, where $L$ is of type LieAlgebra
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Monomials: (Macaulay2Doc)coefficients, => ..., default value
        null,
      * *note Variables: (Macaulay2Doc)coefficients, => ..., default value
        null,
  * Outputs:
      * c, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the lists of coefficients and
        monomials in $x$

Description
===========

The optional inputs given above are not relevant for Lie algebras. A Lie
element $x$ has a normal form in a Lie algebra $L$, which is a linear
combination of basis elements in a certain order; coefficients(x) gives the
lists of coefficients and monomials in this representation. If the Lie element
has been obtained using the "formal" operators, then coefficients(x) gives the
coefficients and monomials for all the iterated Lie products used in the
expression.



+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = lieAlgebra{a,b,c}                    |
|                                              |
|o1 = L                                        |
|                                              |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x = a b c - 3 c b a +(1/3) b a c         |
|                                              |
|o2 =  - (4/3)(b c a) - 2 (c b a)              |
|                                              |
|o2 : L                                        |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : coefficients x                           |
|                                              |
|         4                                    |
|o3 = {{- -, -2}, {(b c a), (c b a)}}          |
|         3                                    |
|                                              |
|o3 : List                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : y = a@b@c/3@c@b@a++(1/3)@b@a@c           |
|                                              |
|o4 = (a b c) - 3 (c b a) + (1/3)(b a c)       |
|                                              |
|o4 : L                                        |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : coefficients y                           |
|                                              |
|              1                               |
|o5 = {{1, -3, -}, {(a b c), (c b a), (b a c)}}|
|              3                               |
|                                              |
|o5 : List                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note monomials(LieElement): monomials_lpLieElement_rp, -- get the
    monomials of a Lie element
  * *note indexForm: indexForm, -- get a Lie element in the polynomial ring
