firstDegree -- get the degree of an element
*******************************************

Description
===========

 The degree of an element $x$ in a Lie algebra or an Ext-algebra is the first
degree of the homogeneous element $x$. The zero element has degree 0; however,
its degree should be thought of as arbitrary. The degree of a Lie derivation
$d$ is the first degree of $d$ considered as a graded map.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        n=firstDegree(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,
  * Outputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,  the first degree of $x$

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        n=firstDegree(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note ExtElement: ExtElement,
  * Outputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,  the first degree of $x$

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        n=firstDegree(d)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an instance of the type *note LieDerivation: LieDerivation,
  * Outputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,  the first degree of $d$
+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = lieAlgebra({a,b,c},Weights=>{1,2,3})|
|                                             |
|o1 = L                                       |
|                                             |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : firstDegree(c a b+a b c)                |
|                                             |
|o2 = 6                                       |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = extAlgebra(5,L)                     |
|                                             |
|o3 = E                                       |
|                                             |
|o3 : ExtAlgebra                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : apply(gens E,firstDegree)               |
|                                             |
|o4 = {1, 2, 3}                               |
|                                             |
|o4 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : d=lieDerivation({a c b,b b c,c c b})    |
|                                             |
|o5 = d                                       |
|                                             |
|o5 : LieDerivation                           |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i6 : firstDegree d                           |
|                                             |
|o6 = 5                                       |
+---------------------------------------------+

See also
========

