holonomy(...,Field=>...) -- optional argument for holonomy
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = holonomy(A,Field => F)
        L = holonomy(A,B,Field => F)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the field of coefficients
      * A, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * B, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, 

Description
===========

This is an option for *note holonomy: holonomy, to define the coefficient
field, which is QQ by default. You may use any "exact" field (not the real
numbers or the complex numbers), such as a prime field or an algebraic
extension, e.g., toField(ZZ/7[x]/ideal\{x^2+1\}) or a fraction field, e.g.,
frac(QQ[x]). Observe that it is necessary to use the function toField when $F$
is defined as an algebraic extension of a prime field.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : F = toField(ZZ/7[x]/ideal{x^2+1})       |
|                                             |
|o1 = F                                       |
|                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = holonomy({{a,d}},{{a,b,c}},Field=>F)|
|                                             |
|o2 = L                                       |
|                                             |
|o2 : LieAlgebra                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (3*x+2) a b + (2*x+3) b a               |
|                                             |
|o3 = (-x+1)(c b)                             |
|                                             |
|o3 : L                                       |
+---------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note lieAlgebra: lieAlgebra, -- make a free Lie algebra
  * *note holonomy: holonomy, -- compute the holonomy Lie algebra associated to
    an arrangement or matroid
  * *note Second Lie algebra tutorial: Second Lie algebra tutorial,
  * *note Holonomy Lie algebras and symmetries: Holonomy Lie algebras and
    symmetries,

Functions with optional argument named Field:
=============================================

  * *note holonomy(...,Field=>...): holonomy_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmField=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
    -- optional argument for holonomy
  * *note lieAlgebra(...,Field=>...):
    lieAlgebra_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmField=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- optional argument for
    lieAlgebra

Further information
===================

  * Default value: *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
  * Function: *note holonomy: holonomy, -- compute the holonomy Lie algebra
    associated to an arrangement or matroid
  * Option key: *note Field: Field, -- name for an optional argument for
    lieAlgebra and holonomy
