holonomyLocal -- compute the Lie algebra for a local subalgebra of the holonomy Lie algebra
*******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = holonomyLocal(i,H)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, referring to the $i$th set,
        where the sets in the first input of holonomy are counted before the
        sets in the second input
      * H, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, the holonomy
        Lie algebra
  * Outputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, the Lie
        subalgebra

Description
===========

The generators in the $i$th set (beginning with $i=0$) in the inputs of *note
holonomy: holonomy, generate a subalgebra of the holonomy Lie algebra $H$, and
the output of holonomyLocal(i,H) is this Lie subalgebra. If the set is of size
$k$, then the local Lie algebra is free on $k$ generators if the set belongs to
the first input set, and it is free on $k-1$ generators in degrees $\ge 2$ if
it belongs to the second input set.





+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : H=holonomy({{a1,a2},{a3,a4}},{{a1,a3,a5},{a2,a4,a5}})|
|                                                          |
|o1 = H                                                    |
|                                                          |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : describe holonomyLocal(1,H)                          |
|                                                          |
|o2 = generators => {a3, a4}                               |
|     Weights => {{1, 0}, {1, 0}}                          |
|     Signs => {0, 0}                                      |
|     ideal => {}                                          |
|     ambient => LieAlgebra{...10...}                      |
|     diff => {}                                           |
|     Field => QQ                                          |
|     computedDegree => 0                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : describe holonomyLocal(2,H)                          |
|                                                          |
|o3 = generators => {a1, a3, a5}                           |
|     Weights => {{1, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 0}}                  |
|     Signs => {0, 0, 0}                                   |
|     ideal => {(a3 a1) - (a5 a3), (a5 a1) + (a5 a3)}      |
|     ambient => LieAlgebra{...10...}                      |
|     diff => {}                                           |
|     Field => QQ                                          |
|     computedDegree => 0                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note holonomy: holonomy, -- compute the holonomy Lie algebra associated to
    an arrangement or matroid
  * *note decompose(LieAlgebra): decompose_lpLieAlgebra_rp, -- compute the
    ideal associated to an arrangement or matroid
  * *note Holonomy Lie algebras and symmetries: Holonomy Lie algebras and
    symmetries,

Ways to use holonomyLocal:
==========================

  * "holonomyLocal(ZZ,LieAlgebra)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note holonomyLocal: holonomyLocal, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

