inverse(LieAlgebraMap,LieSubSpace) -- make the inverse image of a Lie subspace under a Lie algebra map
******************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note inverse: (Macaulay2Doc)inverse,
  * Usage: 
        I=inverse(f,S)
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraMap: LieAlgebraMap,, 
      * S, an instance of the type *note LieSubSpace: LieSubSpace,, an instance
        of type LieSubSpace, a Lie subspace of the target of $f$
  * Outputs:
      * I, an instance of the type *note LieSubSpace: LieSubSpace,, an instance
        of LieSubSpace, a Lie subspace of the source of $f$, the inverse image
        of $S$ under $f$,

Description
===========

If $S$ is an instance of LieIdeal, then $I$ is of type LieIdeal. If $S$ is an
instance of  LieSubAlgebra but not of LieIdeal, then $I$ is of type
LieSubAlgebra. Otherwise, $I$ is of type LieSubSpace.



+--------------------------+
|i1 : F=lieAlgebra{a,b,c}  |
|                          |
|o1 = F                    |
|                          |
|o1 : LieAlgebra           |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : I=lieIdeal{b c - a c}|
|                          |
|o2 = I                    |
|                          |
|o2 : FGLieIdeal           |
+--------------------------+
|i3 : Q=F/I                |
|                          |
|o3 = Q                    |
|                          |
|o3 : LieAlgebra           |
+--------------------------+
|i4 : f=map(Q,F)           |
|                          |
|o4 = f                    |
|                          |
|o4 : LieAlgebraMap        |
+--------------------------+
|i5 : J=lieIdeal{a b}      |
|                          |
|o5 = J                    |
|                          |
|o5 : FGLieIdeal           |
+--------------------------+
|i6 : K=inverse(f,J)       |
|                          |
|o6 = K                    |
|                          |
|o6 : LieIdeal             |
+--------------------------+
|i7 : dims(1,6,F/K)        |
|                          |
|o7 = {3, 1, 2, 3, 6, 9}   |
|                          |
|o7 : List                 |
+--------------------------+
|i8 : dims(1,6,Q/J)        |
|                          |
|o8 = {3, 1, 2, 3, 6, 9}   |
|                          |
|o8 : List                 |
+--------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note inverse(LieDerivation,LieSubSpace):
    inverse_lpLieDerivation_cmLieSubSpace_rp, -- make the inverse image of a
    Lie subspace under a Lie derivation
  * *note image(LieAlgebraMap,LieSubSpace):
    image_lpLieAlgebraMap_cmLieSubSpace_rp, -- make the image of a Lie subspace
    under a Lie algebra map
  * *note kernel(LieAlgebraMap): kernel_lpLieAlgebraMap_rp, -- make the kernel
    of a map

