isSurjective(LieAlgebraMap) -- whether a Lie map is surjective
**************************************************************

  * Function: *note isSurjective: (Macaulay2Doc)isSurjective,
  * Usage: 
        f=isSurjective(f)
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraMap: LieAlgebraMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if $f$ is
        surjective, false otherwise

Description
===========

The map may not be well defined. Use *note isWellDefined(ZZ,LieAlgebraMap):
isWellDefined_lpZZ_cmLieAlgebraMap_rp, to test if the map is well defined.





+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : F=lieAlgebra{a,b,c}                              |
|                                                      |
|o1 = F                                                |
|                                                      |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L=F/{a b,a b c}                                  |
|                                                      |
|o2 = L                                                |
|                                                      |
|o2 : LieAlgebra                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M=minimalModel(3,L)                              |
|                                                      |
|o3 = M                                                |
|                                                      |
|o3 : LieAlgebra                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isSurjective map M                               |
|                                                      |
|o4 = true                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f=map(F,L)                                       |
|warning: the map might not be well defined,           |
|           use isWellDefined                          |
|                                                      |
|o5 = f                                                |
|                                                      |
|o5 : LieAlgebraMap                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isSurjective f                                   |
|                                                      |
|o6 = true                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isWellDefined(3,f)                               |
|the map is not well defined                           |
|the map commutes with the differential for all degrees|
|                                                      |
|o7 = false                                            |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : g=map(L,F)                                       |
|                                                      |
|o8 = g                                                |
|                                                      |
|o8 : LieAlgebraMap                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isSurjective g                                   |
|                                                      |
|o9 = true                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+

