LieAlgebra == LieAlgebra -- whether two Lie algebras are defined in the same way
********************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        L==M
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, 
      * M, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Two objects L and M of type LieAlgebra satisfies L==M if they have the same
generators, weights, signs, field, defining ideal, and differential.



+------------------------+
|i1 : F = lieAlgebra{a,b}|
|                        |
|o1 = F                  |
|                        |
|o1 : LieAlgebra         |
+------------------------+
|i2 : I = lieIdeal{a a b}|
|                        |
|o2 = I                  |
|                        |
|o2 : FGLieIdeal         |
+------------------------+
|i3 : L=F/{a a b}        |
|                        |
|o3 = L                  |
|                        |
|o3 : LieAlgebra         |
+------------------------+
|i4 : M=F/I              |
|                        |
|o4 = M                  |
|                        |
|o4 : LieAlgebra         |
+------------------------+
|i5 : L==M               |
|                        |
|o5 = true               |
+------------------------+
|i6 : L===M              |
|                        |
|o6 = false              |
+------------------------+

