lieAlgebra(...,Field=>...) -- optional argument for lieAlgebra
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = lieAlgebra(gen,Field => F)
  * Inputs:
      * gen, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * F, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the field of coefficients
  * Outputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, 

Description
===========

This is an option for *note lieAlgebra: lieAlgebra, and *note holonomy:
holonomy, to define the coefficient field, which is QQ by default. You may use
any "exact" field (not the real numbers or the complex numbers), such as a
prime field or an algebraic extension, e.g., toField(ZZ/7[x]/ideal\{x^2+1\}) or
a fraction field, e.g., frac(QQ[x]). Observe that it is necessary to use the
function toField when $F$ is defined as an algebraic extension of a prime
field.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : F = toField(ZZ/7[x]/ideal{x^2+1})|
|                                      |
|o1 = F                                |
|                                      |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                   |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = lieAlgebra({a,b},Field=>F)   |
|                                      |
|o2 = L                                |
|                                      |
|o2 : LieAlgebra                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : (3*x+2) a b + (2*x+3) b a        |
|                                      |
|o3 = (-x+1)(b a)                      |
|                                      |
|o3 : L                                |
+--------------------------------------+

