LieAlgebraMap == LieAlgebraMap -- whether two Lie algebra homomorphisms are defined in the same way
***************************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        f==g
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraMap: LieAlgebraMap,, 
      * g, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraMap: LieAlgebraMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Two objects f and g of type LieAlgebraMap satisfies f==g if source f==source g,
target f==target g, and the values of the generators of source f under f
considered as elements in target g are the same as the values of the generators
of source g under g.





+------------------------+
|i1 : F = lieAlgebra{a,b}|
|                        |
|o1 = F                  |
|                        |
|o1 : LieAlgebra         |
+------------------------+
|i2 : I = lieIdeal{a a b}|
|                        |
|o2 = I                  |
|                        |
|o2 : FGLieIdeal         |
+------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(F/I,F)     |
|                        |
|o3 = f                  |
|                        |
|o3 : LieAlgebraMap      |
+------------------------+
|i4 : G = lieAlgebra{a,b}|
|                        |
|o4 = G                  |
|                        |
|o4 : LieAlgebra         |
+------------------------+
|i5 : g=map(G/{a a b},G) |
|                        |
|o5 = g                  |
|                        |
|o5 : LieAlgebraMap      |
+------------------------+
|i6 : f==g               |
|                        |
|o6 = true               |
+------------------------+
|i7 : f===g              |
|                        |
|o7 = false              |
+------------------------+

