map(LieAlgebra,LieAlgebra) -- make a natural Lie algebra homomorphism
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        f=map(L,M)
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, 
      * M, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null,
      * *note DegreeLift: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
      * *note DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraMap: LieAlgebraMap,, a map
        from $M$ to $L$

Description
===========

The optional inputs given above are not relevant for Lie algebras. The effect
of map(L,M) is that the "common" generators are mapped to themselves and the
other generators are mapped to 0 (cf map for rings). Two generators are
"common" if they have the same name and the same weight and sign. The output
map f might not be well defined and not commute with the differentials. It can
be checked whether this is true by using *note isWellDefined(ZZ,LieAlgebraMap):
isWellDefined_lpZZ_cmLieAlgebraMap_rp,.



+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = lieAlgebra{a,b,c}                   |
|                                             |
|o1 = M                                       |
|                                             |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = lieAlgebra({a,b,d},Weights=>{2,1,1})|
|                                             |
|o2 = L                                       |
|                                             |
|o2 : LieAlgebra                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(L,M)                            |
|                                             |
|o3 = f                                       |
|                                             |
|o3 : LieAlgebraMap                           |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : describe f                              |
|                                             |
|o4 = a => 0                                  |
|     b => b                                  |
|     c => 0                                  |
|     source => M                             |
|     target => L                             |
+---------------------------------------------+

