The quasi-isomorphism \ $f:\ M\ \to\ L$ from the minimal model $M$ of $L$ to
$L$ is obtained as map(M). If $L$ has no differential, then \ $f$ \ is
surjective, but in general this is not true as is shown by the example below.
Another example is obtained letting $L$ be a non-zero Lie algebra with zero
homology, see *note Differential Lie algebra tutorial: Differential Lie algebra
tutorial,.



+----------------------------------------+
|i38 :                                   |
|      f = map M                         |
|                                        |
|o38 = f                                 |
|                                        |
