monomials(LieElement) -- get the monomials of a Lie element
***********************************************************

  * Function: *note monomials: (Macaulay2Doc)monomials,
  * Usage: 
        c = monomials(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,, $x$ is of
        type $L$, where $L$ is of type LieAlgebra
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Variables: (Macaulay2Doc)monomials_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariables=>_pd_
        pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * c, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of monomials in $x$

Description
===========

The optional input given above is not relevant for Lie algebras. This is equal
to the second part of *note coefficients(LieElement):
coefficients_lpLieElement_rp,.





+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = lieAlgebra{a,b,c}             |
|                                       |
|o1 = L                                 |
|                                       |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : x = a b c - 3 c b a +(1/3) b a c  |
|                                       |
|o2 =  - (4/3)(b c a) - 2 (c b a)       |
|                                       |
|o2 : L                                 |
