normalForm -- compute the normal form of a LieElement
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        c = normalForm(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,, $x$ is of
        type $L$, where $L$ is of type LieAlgebra
  * Outputs:
      * c, an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,, the normal
        form of $x$

Description
===========

A Lie element obtained as a linear combination of iterated Lie products of
generators has an output that is of normal form. If the Lie element is defined
by the "formal" operators, then the output may be of non-normal form, and in
this case, the normal form is obtained using normalForm.



+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = lieAlgebra{a,b,c}             |
|                                       |
|o1 = L                                 |
|                                       |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : x = a b c - 3 c b a +(1/3) b a c  |
|                                       |
|o2 =  - (4/3)(b c a) - 2 (c b a)       |
|                                       |
|o2 : L                                 |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : y = a@b@c/3@c@b@a++(1/3)@b@a@c    |
|                                       |
|o3 = (a b c) - 3 (c b a) + (1/3)(b a c)|
|                                       |
|o3 : L                                 |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : normalForm y                      |
|                                       |
|o4 =  - (4/3)(b c a) - 2 (c b a)       |
|                                       |
|o4 : L                                 |
+---------------------------------------+

