In L#cache there is more information about $L$ collected during a computation.
Some parts of the information are visible to the user, e.g., *note lieRing:
lieRing, and *note mbRing: mbRing,. The ring L#cache.lieRing is the internal
polynomial ring representation of Lie elements. The Lie monomials are
represented as commutative monomials in this ring. The program produces
internally an ideal of relations and a basis, which may be seen as L#cache.gb
and L#cache.basis. The number of generators in *note lieRing: lieRing, is the
number of generators in the Lie algebra times the internal counter L#cache.max,
which initially is set to $5$, and is changed to $n+5$ if the computation of
$L$ is performed up to degree $n$ with $n\ >$ L#cache.max.



