sign(LieElement) -- get the sign of a homogeneous element  
***********************************************************

  * Function: *note sign: (Macaulay2Doc)sign,

Description
===========

The sign of a homogeneous Lie (or Ext) element $x$ is obtained as sign(x). The
zero element has sign equal to 0; however, its sign should be thought of as
arbitrary. The sign of a derivation $d$ is the sign of $d$ as a graded map and
may also be obtained as d#sign.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        s=sign(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,, an element of
        type $L$ where $L$ is of type LieAlgebra
  * Outputs:
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the sign; 0 or 1
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = lieAlgebra({a,b,c},Weights=>{{1,0},{2,1},{3,2}},       |
|         LastWeightHomological=>true, Signs => 1)               |
|                                                                |
|o1 = L                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D=differentialLieAlgebra{0_L,a a,a b}/{a a b, a a c, b a b}|
|                                                                |
|o2 = D                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o2 : LieAlgebra                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x=a b c+2 c b a                                            |
|                                                                |
|o3 =  - 2 (b a c) - (a b c)                                     |
|                                                                |
|o3 : D                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : sign x                                                     |
|                                                                |
|o4 = 1                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        s=sign(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note ExtElement: ExtElement,, an element of
        type $E$ where $E$ is of type ExtAlgebra
  * Outputs:
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the sign; 0 or 1
+----------------------+
|i5 : E=extAlgebra(5,D)|
|                      |
|o5 = E                |
|                      |
|o5 : ExtAlgebra       |
+----------------------+
|i6 : b=basis(5,E)     |
|                      |
|o6 = {ext_4, ext_5}   |
|                      |
|o6 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i7 : apply(b,sign)    |
|                      |
|o7 = {1, 1}           |
|                      |
|o7 : List             |
+----------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        s=sign(d)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an instance of the type *note LieDerivation: LieDerivation,
  * Outputs:
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the sign; 0 or 1
+------------------------+
|i8 : sign differential D|
|                        |
|o8 = 1                  |
+------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note firstDegree(LieElement): firstDegree, -- get the degree of an element
  * *note weight: weight, -- get the weight of a homogeneous element

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "sign(ExtElement)"
  * "sign(LieDerivation)"
  * *note sign(LieElement): sign_lpLieElement_rp, -- get the sign of a
    homogeneous element
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

