standardForm(RingElement,LieAlgebra) -- get a Lie element in standard form
**************************************************************************

  * Function: *note standardForm: (Macaulay2Doc)standardForm,

Description
===========

The set of linear polynomials in L#cache.mbRing gives a representation of Lie
elements. The function standardForm gives back the standard output and
indexForm goes in the other direction.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        standardForm(r,L)
  * Inputs:
      * r, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element in
        L#cache.mbRing
      * L, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,, the
        corresponding Lie element

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        standardForm(x,L)
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of elements in
        L#cache.mbRing
      * L, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of the corresponding Lie
        elements
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = lieAlgebra{a,b}                               |
|                                                       |
|o1 = L                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : b3 = basis(3,L)                                   |
|                                                       |
|o2 = {(a b a), (b b a)}                                |
|                                                       |
|o2 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = L#cache.mbRing                                |
|                                                       |
|o3 = Q                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : gens Q                                            |
|                                                       |
|o4 = {mb      , mb      , mb      , mb      , mb      }|
|        {1, 0}    {1, 1}    {2, 0}    {3, 0}    {3, 1} |
|                                                       |
|o4 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : c3 = {indexForm a a b,indexForm b a b}            |
|                                                       |
|o5 = {-mb      , -mb      }                            |
|         {3, 0}     {3, 1}                             |
|                                                       |
|o5 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : standardForm(c3,L)                                |
|                                                       |
|o6 = { - (a b a),  - (b b a)}                          |
|                                                       |
|o6 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : standardForm(mb_{3,0}+2*mb_{3,1},L)               |
|                                                       |
|o7 = (a b a) + 2 (b b a)                               |
|                                                       |
|o7 : L                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : indexForm oo                                      |
|                                                       |
|o8 = mb       + 2mb                                    |
|       {3, 0}      {3, 1}                              |
|                                                       |
|o8 : Q                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note indexForm: indexForm, -- get a Lie element in the polynomial ring
    representation
  * *note mbRing: mbRing, -- a polynomial ring representation of the Lie
    algebra used for output
  * *note normalForm: normalForm, -- compute the normal form of a LieElement

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "standardForm(List,LieAlgebra)"
  * *note standardForm(RingElement,LieAlgebra):
    standardForm_lpRingElement_cmLieAlgebra_rp, -- get a Lie element in
    standard form
