weight -- get the weight of a homogeneous element
*************************************************

Description
===========

The weight of a homogeneous Lie (or Ext) element $x$ is obtained as weight(x).
The zero element of a Lie algebra has weight equal to a list of zeroes of
length equal to the degree length of the Lie algebra; however, its weight
should be thought of as arbitrary. The weight of a derivation $d$ is the weight
of $d$ as a graded map and may also be obtained as d#weight.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        w=weight(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note LieElement: LieElement,
  * Outputs:
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = lieAlgebra({a,b,c},Weights=>{{1,0},{2,1},{3,2}},       |
|         LastWeightHomological=>true, Signs => 1)               |
|                                                                |
|o1 = L                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o1 : LieAlgebra                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D=differentialLieAlgebra{0_L,a a,a b}/{a a b, a a c, b a b}|
|                                                                |
|o2 = D                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o2 : LieAlgebra                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x=a b c+2 c b a                                            |
|                                                                |
|o3 =  - 2 (b a c) - (a b c)                                     |
|                                                                |
|o3 : D                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : weight x                                                   |
|                                                                |
|o4 = {6, 3}                                                     |
|                                                                |
|o4 : List                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : weight 0_D                                                 |
|                                                                |
|o5 = {0, 0}                                                     |
|                                                                |
|o5 : List                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        w=weight(x)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note ExtElement: ExtElement,
  * Outputs:
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
+----------------------+
|i6 : E=extAlgebra(5,D)|
|                      |
|o6 = E                |
|                      |
|o6 : ExtAlgebra       |
+----------------------+
|i7 : b=basis(5,E)     |
|                      |
|o7 = {ext_4, ext_5}   |
|                      |
|o7 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i8 : apply(b,weight)  |
|                      |
|o8 = {{5, 4}, {5, 4}} |
|                      |
|o8 : List             |
+----------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        w=weight(d)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an instance of the type *note LieDerivation: LieDerivation,
  * Outputs:
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
+--------------------------+
|i9 : weight differential D|
|                          |
|o9 = {0, -1}              |
|                          |
|o9 : List                 |
+--------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note firstDegree(LieElement): firstDegree, -- get the degree of an element
  * *note sign(LieElement): sign_lpLieElement_rp, -- get the sign of a
    homogeneous element
  * *note degreeLength: (Macaulay2Doc)degreeLength, -- the length of the degree
    vector

Ways to use weight:
===================

  * "weight(ExtElement)"
  * "weight(LieDerivation)"
  * "weight(LieElement)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note weight: weight, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

